# Line endings, decided by the repository rather than by each clone.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is a per-host setting, and this project's tooling cannot rely
# on it: the worktree had 279 CRLF files next to 104 LF ones, and every commit
# printed "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings, which trains a reader to
# ignore git's output. The index is LF throughout; this keeps it that way, so a
# fresh clone on Windows and one on Linux hold identical bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The one exception, and it is the platform's: the PowerShell helpers under
# `tools/sdd/` are run by Windows PowerShell, whose own tooling expects CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
